meta {
  name: Customer_Order
}

auth {
  mode: apikey
}

auth:apikey {
  key: X-Customer-Auth-Token
  value: {{customerToken}}
  placement: header
}

docs {
  Orders of a signed-in customer: the customer token goes to `X-Customer-Auth-Token`. Get it with `Customer_Auth` sign-in or confirm.
  
  Scenario, in `seq` order:
  
  1. `Place the order` — from the selected cart items and the checkout choice (`Customer_Cart`: add an item, choose the address, delivery and payment). Saves `customerOrderId`.
  2. `Show my order` — the card: `payment_url` (open it to pay on the site; open it again to repeat a failed payment), `is_paid` (no notification: poll this request), delivery, address and recipient, items with images, `status_history`.
  3. `List my orders` — the same cards, newest first, `status` filters by one status.
  4. `Cancel my order` — an unpaid order only; a paid one gives 409 `order-already-paid`. Run it to clean up the order of the scenario.
}
